\ the hood: the windscreen raked straight back from its base to the hood's top, a triangle of glass each side and the flat front panel between them, its base across, its rear edges and top joined to the hood's front frame by glass; the sliding hood's four frames, flat-sided with a bar across each side and a flat top, each leaning back 0.09 m from its sill to its top, joined along the sills, the bars and the top's corners, glazed between them, the glass without lines of its own and the frames, sills and bars drawn just outside it, so its panes show; the solid fairing behind it is the fuselage's (heights and positions measured on the side and plan views of the Mk I three-view by M. L. Watts, scaled to the published 9.55 m length)
