\ the undercarriage: each leg an oleo 9 cm square in Sky standing straight down from the centre section, braced inboard to the wing's underside 0.95 m out from 0.4 m down it, as a photograph of a Hurricane in flight shows, the wheel on its inboard side for the published track of 7 ft 10 in, the leg's cover in Sky outboard of it, 8 cm thick, narrow at the wing, its front edge slanting far forward down to a long bottom edge just above the hub over the tyre's top, its rear edge dropping nearly straight and stepping back at the bottom (the wheel's size and place and the leg's measured on the side and front views of the Mk I three-view by M. L. Watts; the door's shape from a photograph)
