\ a roundel painted on each side of a body of rings of a number of sides: a disc for each radius from the largest, in its colour, about a station along and a height up, its rings at each sixth of its radius each 48 points laid 2 cm off the skin, filled between them from its centre so it bends round the body's corners, each disc 1 cm prouder than the one before, without lines of its own
