	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ 2.12 1.92 1.72 ] ( along |
			model [ [ side 0.57 * 0.16 along ] [ side 0.57 * 0.16 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.04 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.04 along ] ] [ 0 0.1 along ] exhaust-colour sketch-painted-plate
			model [ [ side 0.47 * 0.16 along ] [ side 0.47 * 0.16 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.16 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.16 along ] ] [ 0 0 along ] exhaust-colour sketch-painted-plate
			model [ [ side 0.47 * 0.04 along ] [ side 0.47 * 0.04 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.04 along 0.18 - ] [ side 0.57 * 0.04 along ] ] [ 0 0.2 along ] exhaust-colour sketch-painted-plate
		) each
	) each
	model sketch-hurricane-hood
	model sketch-hurricane-wings
	model@faces size to tub-first-face
	model hurricane-radiator-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 10 sketch-body
	tub-first-face model@faces size 1 do k model@faces k @i sky-paint-colour add-last! drop loop
	model hurricane-intake-ring [ 0 0 0 ] 16 body-ring [ 0 -1.02 -0.3 ] radiator-intake-colour sketch-painted-plate
	model hurricane-keel ( pair | [ 0 pair second pair first ] ) map sky-paint-colour sketch-plate
	model sketch-hurricane-tail-wheel
	model hurricane-tailplane [ hurricane-elevator ] 0 0.15 hurricane-tailplane-half-thickness sketch-thick-surface
	model 0 hurricane-fin hurricane-rudder hurricane-fin-half-thickness sketch-thick-fin
	model hurricane-mast null sketch-plate
	model hurricane-aerial sketch-path
	model hurricane-fin-flash hurricane-fin-half-thickness sketch-fin-flash
	model hurricane-dark-earth 0.55 6.095 ' hurricane-skin sketch-dark-earth
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		side 4.2 * to out
		model out [ hurricane-roundel-radius hurricane-roundel-centre-radius ] [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-red-colour ] ' hurricane-skin ' hurricane-edges-at sketch-wing-roundel
	) each
	model hurricane-rings 10 hurricane-fuselage-roundel-along hurricane-fuselage-roundel-up hurricane-fuselage-roundel-radii
	[ roundel-yellow-colour roundel-blue-colour roundel-white-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-skin-roundel
	wheels-down if model sketch-hurricane-undercarriage then
	model ;

: hurricane-model ( wheels-down -- model ) hurricane-sketch dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ a Hurricane's squadron code, its own letter and, unless empty, its serial near the tail
: sketch-hurricane-markings ( sketch code letter serial -- )
	| sketch code letter serial |
	sketch hurricane-rings 10 hurricane-fuselage-roundel-along hurricane-fuselage-roundel-radii first hurricane-code-letter-up
	code letter serial hurricane-serial-along hurricane-serial-up sketch-markings ;

\ a fighter of a kind, :spitfire or :hurricane, wheels up or down, in a squadron's code and its own letter; the plain model where the code is empty
: marked-model ( kind code letter wheels-down -- model )
	| kind code letter wheels-down |
	kind :hurricane = if wheels-down hurricane-sketch else wheels-down spitfire-sketch then to model
	code size 0 > if
		kind :hurricane = if model code letter "" sketch-hurricane-markings else model code letter "" sketch-spitfire-markings then
	then
	model dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ === the Lysander ===

\ the Westland Lysander Mk II, the mark No. 614 Squadron flew on its coastal patrols from Scotland in 1940, its sleeve-valve Perseus XII in a smooth cowling; the airframe measured on the side, front and plan views of a three-view signed A. V., 2008, at its metre bar's 96.9 pixels a metre, which gives the published span and length, 15.24 m and 9.30 m; metres from a point 2.65 m behind the spinner's point, about the quarter chord of the wing where it is widest, and up from the thrust line

\ the distances out at which the wing's outline and depth are traced, from the root at the canopy's side to the tip's end
[ 0.45 1.0 2.0 2.8 3.0 4.0 5.0 6.0 7.0 7.2 7.4 7.5 7.6 7.65 7.67 ] constant lysander-wing-stations

\ the wing's leading and trailing edges at a distance out, traced on the plan view: the leading edge straight from 2.8 m out to the tip and curving back to the root, the trailing edge straight to 2.8 m out and coming forward beyond it, the tip rounded
: lysander-edges-at ( out -- leading trailing )
	| out |
	out abs to distance
	lysander-wing-stations [ 0.07 0.15 0.35 0.48 0.49 0.50 0.50 0.50 0.51 0.51 0.50 0.49 0.43 0.32 0.26 ] distance table-at
	lysander-wing-stations [ -1.52 -1.52 -1.52 -1.52 -1.45 -1.32 -1.05 -0.79 -0.50 -0.39 -0.21 -0.09 0.04 0.20 0.26 ] distance table-at ;

\ the wing's flat underside's height at a distance out, measured on the front view: rising 5 cm from the root to the strut, 3.06 m out, and 0.31 m more to the tip; the whole set 0.15 m higher than the front view draws it, where the colour profile puts the wing on the canopy's roof
: lysander-underside-at ( out -- up )
	| out |
	[ 0.45 3.06 7.67 ] [ 1.15 1.20 1.51 ] out abs table-at ;

\ the wing's depth at a distance out, measured on the front view: 0.16 m at the root, 0.34 m at the strut, 0.10 m at 7.4 m out, closing round the tip
: lysander-depth-at ( out -- depth )
	| out |
	[ 0.45 3.06 7.4 7.67 ] [ 0.16 0.34 0.10 0.04 ] out abs table-at ;

\ the point on the wing's upper surface a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge, the section the Hurricane's Clark YH over its flat underside (an estimate)
: lysander-skin ( out share -- point )
	| out share |
	out lysander-edges-at to trailing to leading
	hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair first ) map hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair second ) map share table-at to rise
	[ out out lysander-underside-at out lysander-depth-at rise * + leading leading trailing - share * - ] ;

\ the point on the wing's underside a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge
: lysander-underside ( out share -- point )
	| out share |
	out lysander-edges-at to trailing to leading
	[ out out lysander-underside-at leading leading trailing - share * - ] ;

\ the wings: a rib at every station, its upper surface over the flat underside at the section's shares of the chord, the skin filled between each rib and the next above and below, the root's rib closed against the canopy, the ribs and the edges kept as lines; a Type B roundel on each upper wing, the Hurricane's, 5.2 m out (an estimate)
: sketch-lysander-wings ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair first ) map to shares
	shares size to n-shares
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		lysander-wing-stations ( out | sketch shares ( share | side out * share lysander-skin ) map sketch-points ) map to uppers
		lysander-wing-stations ( out | sketch shares ( share | side out * share lysander-underside ) map sketch-points ) map to lowers
		uppers ( rib | sketch rib join-path ) each
		sketch uppers ( rib | rib first ) map join-path
		sketch uppers ( rib | rib last ) map join-path
		0 lysander-wing-stations size 1- 1 do r
			lysander-wing-stations r @i lysander-wing-stations r 1+ @i + 2 / side * to middle-out
			middle-out 0.3 lysander-skin middle-out 0.3 lysander-underside v+ 0.5 v* to inside
			0 n-shares 1- 1 do j
				sketch [ uppers r @i j @i uppers r @i j 1+ @i uppers r 1+ @i j 1+ @i uppers r 1+ @i j @i ] inside sketch-face
				sketch [ lowers r @i j @i lowers r @i j 1+ @i lowers r 1+ @i j 1+ @i lowers r 1+ @i j @i ] inside sketch-face
			loop
		loop
		sketch uppers first lowers first reverse concat [ side 0.8 * 1.1 0 ] sketch-face
		sketch side 5.2 * [ hurricane-roundel-radius hurricane-roundel-centre-radius ] [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-red-colour ] ' lysander-skin ' lysander-edges-at sketch-wing-roundel
	) each ;

\ the spinner, 0.46 m long and 0.50 m across, on the cowling's centre line 0.10 m above the thrust line, so 0.13 m of the propeller's shaft shows behind it, as a colour profile of a Lysander draws them
: lysander-spinner-rings ( -- rings ) [ [ 2.65 0.02 0.02 0.10 ] [ 2.6 0.12 0.12 0.10 ] [ 2.52 0.19 0.19 0.10 ] [ 2.40 0.235 0.235 0.10 ] [ 2.28 0.25 0.25 0.10 ] [ 2.19 0.25 0.25 0.10 ] ] ;

\ the fuselage from the cowling's lip to the tail as rings, their centres level on the cowling's centre line, 0.10 m above the thrust line, so the lines along the fuselage run straight, each ring's halves reaching its top and bottom: the Perseus's round cowling 1.4 m across; the deck behind it falling under the windscreen to the cockpits' sills; the underside straight 0.60 m below the thrust line from the cowling to 4.0 m behind the spinner's point, then curving up to the tail; the rear fuselage's top rising behind the gunner's cockpit along the canopy's raked rear edge and falling straight to the fin; heights measured on a colour profile of a Lysander scaled to the three-view's length, widths on the three-view's plan view, those under the wing estimates
: lysander-rings ( -- rings )
	[ [ 2.07 0.58 0.57 0.10 0.59 ] [ 1.95 0.68 0.66 0.10 0.68 ] [ 1.65 0.70 0.70 0.10 0.70 ] [ 1.05 0.68 0.70 0.10 0.69 ] [ 0.65 0.62 0.70 0.10 0.64 ]
	  [ -0.35 0.60 0.71 0.10 0.51 ] [ -1.35 0.62 0.71 0.10 0.47 ] [ -2.18 0.64 0.68 0.10 0.48 ] [ -2.60 0.61 0.66 0.10 0.99 ]
	  [ -2.85 0.59 0.64 0.10 0.93 ] [ -3.35 0.555 0.59 0.10 0.86 ] [ -3.85 0.495 0.53 0.10 0.79 ] [ -4.35 0.425 0.45 0.10 0.71 ]
	  [ -4.85 0.33 0.38 0.10 0.63 ] [ -5.35 0.25 0.35 0.10 0.55 ] [ -5.85 0.185 0.26 0.10 0.47 ] [ -6.35 0.11 0.21 0.10 0.35 ] [ -6.65 0.06 0.18 0.10 0.15 ] ] ;

\ the canopy over both cockpits, as [ along top half-width-at-top half-width-at-sill glass-sill ] from the rear: the windscreen's front frame rising from the cowling's rear top, 0.76 m up, to the wing's root, 1.28 m up, and the roof level under the wing, 0.92 m wide there so the wings' roots meet it as the front view draws them, falling behind the wing to the rear edge, raked back 0.40 m from its sill to its top; the glass above a straight sill 0.61 m up from the rear edge to the windscreen; the solid plate in the glass's lower front corner, from the cowling's top up the windscreen's frame to 0.93 m and its rear edge falling steeply to the sill; sides of skin from the glass's sill down to the fuselage's skin 0.45 m up, meeting it along one line rather than passing through it; and the frames' stations; heights and stations from the colour profile, widths from the three-view's front view
[ [ -2.20 1.09 0.40 0.45 0.61 ] [ -1.85 1.19 0.46 0.46 0.61 ] [ -1.52 1.28 0.46 0.46 0.61 ] [ 0.07 1.31 0.46 0.46 0.61 ] [ 0.51 1.28 0.40 0.44 0.61 ]
  [ 0.60 1.16 0.40 0.44 0.61 ] [ 0.77 0.93 0.38 0.44 0.93 ] [ 1.11 0.76 0.38 0.44 0.76 ] ] constant lysander-canopy
0.45 constant lysander-skin-foot
0.40 constant lysander-canopy-rake
[ 0.38 -0.22 -0.57 -0.85 -1.08 -1.81 -2.09 ] constant lysander-canopy-frames

\ the canopy's section at a station along, its widths spread by a factor, its top raised by a height and set back by a distance: on the left the skin's foot on the fuselage and the glass's sill, the top's on the left and the right, on the right the glass's sill and the skin's foot
: lysander-canopy-section ( along spread rise rake -- points )
	| along spread rise rake |
	lysander-canopy ( row | row first ) map to stations
	stations lysander-canopy ( row | row second ) map along table-at rise + to top
	stations lysander-canopy ( row | row 2 @i ) map along table-at spread * to top-half-width
	stations lysander-canopy ( row | row 3 @i ) map along table-at spread * to sill-half-width
	stations lysander-canopy ( row | row 4 @i ) map along table-at to glass-sill
	along rake - to top-along
	[ lysander-rings 12 along lysander-skin-foot -1 0 ring-side-point [ sill-half-width negate glass-sill along ] [ top-half-width negate top top-along ]
	  [ top-half-width top top-along ] [ sill-half-width glass-sill along ] lysander-rings 12 along lysander-skin-foot 1 0 ring-side-point ] ;

\ the rake of the canopy's section at a row: the rearmost row's, the others none
: lysander-row-rake ( index -- rake ) 0 = if lysander-canopy-rake else 0 then ;

\ the canopy: its sides, roof and windscreen glazed without lines of their own, or left open for the view from inside it, the slab sides below the glass and the plate across its front in the object's colour, and its frames, the sills and the roof's edges drawn 3% outside the glass
: sketch-lysander-canopy ( sketch glazed -- )
	| sketch glazed |
	glass-colour unoutlined + to paint
	[ 0 lysander-canopy size 1 do k sketch lysander-canopy k @i first 1 0 k lysander-row-rake lysander-canopy-section sketch-points loop ] to sections
	0 sections size 1- 1 do k
		sections k @i to aft
		sections k 1+ @i to fore
		[ 0 0.6 lysander-canopy k @i first lysander-canopy k 1+ @i first + 2 / ] to inside
		[ lysander-canopy k @i lysander-canopy k 1+ @i ] ( row | row 4 @i row second < ) map spread or to segment-glazed
		0 5 1 do c
			[ aft c @i aft c 1+ @i fore c 1+ @i fore c @i ] to corners
			c 0 = c 4 = or segment-glazed not or if sketch corners inside sketch-face else glazed if sketch corners inside paint sketch-painted-face then then
		loop
	loop
	sketch sections last [ 0 0.5 0 ] sketch-face
	( section | [ section 1 @i section 2 @i section 3 @i section 4 @i ] ) to glazed
	lysander-canopy-frames ( along | sketch along 1.03 0.01 0 lysander-canopy-section glazed execute sketch-path ) each
	sketch lysander-canopy first first 1.03 0.01 lysander-canopy-rake lysander-canopy-section glazed execute sketch-path
	1 5 1 do c
		sketch [ 0 lysander-canopy size 1 do k lysander-canopy k @i first 1.03 0.01 k lysander-row-rake lysander-canopy-section c @i loop ] sketch-path
	loop ;

\ the wheel's fairing, as rings about a line 1.40 m out, from 1.53 m to 3.31 m behind the spinner's point, 0.44 m wide, over the wheel's upper half, from the side and front views
: lysander-fairing-rings ( -- rings )
	[ [ 1.12 0.04 0.04 -1.6 ] [ 1.0 0.16 0.25 -1.62 0.30 ] [ 0.8 0.21 0.28 -1.6 0.5 ] [ 0.45 0.22 0.30 -1.6 0.65 ] [ 0.05 0.22 0.30 -1.6 0.62 ] [ -0.30 0.18 0.22 -1.55 0.45 ] [ -0.66 0.03 0.03 -1.62 ] ] ;

\ the undercarriage, fixed: each leg a broad trouser from the fuselage's underside out and down into the wheel's fairing, 0.56 m fore and aft and 0.14 m thick; the wheel 0.88 m across, its axle 1.90 m below the thrust line; the wing's strut from the underside 3.03 m out down to the trouser's root, 0.16 m fore and aft and 6 cm thick; the tail wheel 0.30 m across on its leg, where the colour profile puts it; from the side and front views, the thicknesses estimates
: sketch-lysander-undercarriage ( sketch -- )
	| sketch |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch lysander-fairing-rings [ side 1.40 * 0 0 ] 12 sketch-body
		sketch [ side 0.43 * -0.50 0.25 ] [ side 1.35 * -1.15 0.25 ] 0.07 0.28 null sketch-bar
		sketch [ side 3.03 * 3.03 lysander-underside-at -0.89 ] [ side 0.62 * -0.62 0.18 ] 0.03 0.08 null sketch-bar
		sketch [ side 1.40 * -1.90 0.45 ] [ side 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] 0.44 0.20 0.4 sketch-wheel
	) each
	sketch [ 0 -0.22 -5.25 ] [ 0 -0.51 -5.47 ] 0.03 hub-colour sketch-strut
	sketch [ 0 -0.51 -5.47 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] 0.15 0.08 0.4 sketch-wheel ;

\ the tailplane from the plan view, as [ out along ], 0.12 m below the thrust line as the side view sets it, the elevators' hinge straight across; the fin and rudder from the side view, as [ along up ], and the rudder's hinge; their half-thicknesses (estimates)
: lysander-tailplane ( -- pairs ) [ [ 0 -4.75 ] [ 1.0 -5.0 ] [ 1.5 -5.18 ] [ 1.75 -5.30 ] [ 1.9 -5.43 ] [ 1.98 -5.65 ] [ 1.95 -5.90 ] [ 1.85 -6.10 ] [ 1.5 -6.32 ] [ 1.0 -6.41 ] [ 0 -6.48 ] ] ;
: lysander-fin ( -- pairs ) [ [ -4.30 0.40 ] [ -4.30 0.70 ] [ -4.56 1.14 ] [ -4.87 1.56 ] [ -5.13 1.92 ] [ -5.46 2.20 ] [ -5.75 2.12 ] [ -6.16 1.76 ] [ -6.37 1.25 ] [ -6.55 0.53 ] [ -6.68 -0.09 ] [ -6.68 -0.20 ] ] ;
: lysander-rudder ( -- pairs ) [ [ -5.56 2.0 ] [ -5.96 -0.25 ] ] ;
0.05 constant lysander-tailplane-half-thickness
0.04 constant lysander-fin-half-thickness

\ the fin flash: red, white and blue each 0.20 m wide ending 7 cm ahead of the rudder's hinge, from 0.75 m up to where the leading edge crosses the red's front (estimates)
: lysander-fin-flash ( -- stripes )
	[ [ -4.95 0.75 ] [ -4.95 1.67 ] ] -5.15 -5.35 -5.55 fin-flash ;

\ the Lysander Mk II: the fuselage, the Perseus's smooth cowling, the black spinner on its hub 0.28 m across, and the turning propeller's disc 3.18 m across, the Perseus's face dark inside the cowling's lip, the canopy, glazed or left open, the high gull wings with their roundels, the struts, the trousered undercarriage and the tail wheel, the tailplane, the fin and rudder with the fin flash, and a Type A1 roundel 35 in across on each side of the rear fuselage; in Dark Green above and Sky beneath, without the Dark Earth's pattern
: lysander-sketch ( glazed -- sketch )
	| glazed |
	new-model-sketch sky-paint-colour :under-colour ! spitfire-under-turn :under-turn ! to model
	model lysander-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 12 sketch-body
	model@faces size to spinner-first-face
	model lysander-spinner-rings [ 0 0 0 ] 12 sketch-body
	model [ [ 2.20 0.14 0.14 0.10 ] [ 2.05 0.14 0.14 0.10 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 12 sketch-body
	spinner-first-face model@faces size 1 do k model@faces k @i spinner-colour add-last! drop loop
	model [ 0 0.10 2.06 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] 0.5 24 ring-of [ 0 0.10 1.5 ] radiator-intake-colour sketch-painted-plate
	model [ 0 0.10 2.23 ] 1.59 sketch-propeller-disc
	model glazed sketch-lysander-canopy
	model sketch-lysander-wings
	model sketch-lysander-undercarriage
	model lysander-tailplane [ [ [ 0 -5.89 ] [ 1.95 -5.89 ] ] ] 0 -0.12 lysander-tailplane-half-thickness sketch-thick-surface
	model 0 lysander-fin lysander-rudder lysander-fin-half-thickness sketch-thick-fin
	model lysander-fin-flash lysander-fin-half-thickness sketch-fin-flash
	model lysander-rings 12 -3.25 0.15 [ 0.445 0.318 0.191 0.064 ] [ roundel-yellow-colour roundel-blue-colour roundel-white-colour roundel-red-colour ] sketch-skin-roundel
	model ;

: lysander-model ( -- model ) true lysander-sketch dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ the Lysander as its pilot sees it from inside the canopy, the glass left out so the view through it is clear
: lysander-cockpit-model ( -- model ) false lysander-sketch dark-green-colour sketch>object ;

\ === the Gladiator ===

\ The Gloster Gladiator Mk II, the mark the Fighter Flight Sumburgh flew
\ over Shetland in 1940, its Mercury VIII in a short cowling open at the
\ front; built to the published span and length, 9.83 m and 8.36 m, the
\ airframe measured on the-blueprints.com's Gladiator three-view: the plan
\ and underside views at 84 px/m for the span, the side view at 117 px/m
\ for the length, its thrust line through the spinner's centre; metres from
\ a point 2.53 m behind the propeller's hub on the thrust line. The side
\ view draws the wings in perspective, so their chords, stagger and tips
\ come from the plan view and their heights from the struts' ends.

4.94 constant gladiator-half-span
1.68 constant gladiator-chord
1.51 constant gladiator-upper-leading
0.75 constant gladiator-lower-leading
1.00 constant gladiator-upper-height
-0.66 constant gladiator-lower-height
0.42 constant gladiator-lower-root
1.6 PI 180 / * tan constant gladiator-dihedral
3 PI 180 / * tan constant gladiator-lower-dihedral
\ the wings' depth, the Clark YH section's 11.7% of the chord (the section an estimate, Gloster's Gauntlet and Gladiator wings being drawn with that flat underside)
0.19 constant gladiator-depth

\ the shares of the chord the leading edge gives up behind the straight and the trailing edge ahead of it at the tip's stations: both corners round over the last 0.7 m of span, the trailing one a little sooner, to the tip's end at mid-chord 4.94 m out; the leading corner measured row by row on the plan view, the trailing on the underside view
: gladiator-tip-shares ( out -- lead trail )
	| out |
	out abs to distance
	distance 4.25 <= if 0 0 exit then
	[ 4.25 4.38 4.46 4.55 4.63 4.71 4.76 4.80 4.83 4.86 4.89 4.91 4.93 4.94 ] [ 0 0.04 0.07 0.10 0.13 0.17 0.21 0.24 0.27 0.30 0.33 0.37 0.41 0.5 ] distance table-at
	[ 4.25 4.38 4.46 4.55 4.63 4.71 4.76 4.80 4.83 4.86 4.89 4.91 4.93 4.94 ] [ 0 0.07 0.10 0.14 0.17 0.23 0.27 0.30 0.33 0.35 0.40 0.44 0.49 0.5 ] distance table-at ;

\ the lower wing's root cut-out, its trailing edge curving forward from the full chord 1.49 m out to 0.29 m ahead of it at the fuselage's side, steepest a third of the way in and flattening toward the fuselage: the share of the depth given up against the share of the way in, measured row by row on the underside view's black port wing; the upper wing's centre cut-out, a half-ellipse 0.26 m wide each side of the centre line and 0.20 m deep round the windscreen, from the plan view's glazing
1.49 constant gladiator-cut-out-span
0.34 constant gladiator-cut-out-depth
: gladiator-cut-out-share ( share -- share ) [ 0 0.07 0.2 0.34 0.39 0.56 0.68 0.87 1 ] [ 0 0.03 0.24 0.44 0.5 0.59 0.71 0.79 0.85 ] rot table-at ;
0.26 constant gladiator-centre-cut-out-span
0.20 constant gladiator-centre-cut-out-depth

\ a wing's leading and trailing edges at a distance out, from its root's leading edge along: straight to 4.25 m out, then round the tip; the lower wing's trailing edge, known by its leading edge, cut forward at the root
: gladiator-edges-at ( out leading -- leading trailing )
	| out leading |
	out gladiator-tip-shares to trail-share to lead-share
	leading lead-share gladiator-chord * - to lead
	leading gladiator-chord - trail-share gladiator-chord * + to trail
	leading gladiator-lower-leading = out abs gladiator-cut-out-span < and if
		gladiator-cut-out-span out abs - gladiator-cut-out-span gladiator-lower-root - / to share
		trail share gladiator-cut-out-share gladiator-cut-out-depth * + to trail
	then
	leading gladiator-upper-leading = out abs gladiator-centre-cut-out-span < and if
		trail 1 out gladiator-centre-cut-out-span / sq - sqrt gladiator-centre-cut-out-depth * + to trail
	then
	lead trail ;

\ a wing's flat underside's height at a distance out, from its height at the root, rising at its dihedral: 1.6° on the upper wing and 3° on the lower, from the front view
: gladiator-height-at ( out height -- up ) | out height | out abs height gladiator-lower-height = if gladiator-lower-dihedral else gladiator-dihedral then * height + ;

\ a wing's depth at a distance out, the section's to 4.25 m out and closing round the tip as the chord does
: gladiator-depth-at ( out -- depth ) gladiator-tip-shares drop 2 * 1 swap - 0 max2 gladiator-depth * ;

\ the point on a wing's upper surface a distance out and a share of the chord back from the leading edge, the Clark YH section over the flat underside, the wing given by its root's leading edge along and its underside's height at the root
: gladiator-skin ( out share leading height -- point )
	| out share leading height |
	out leading gladiator-edges-at to trailing to lead
	hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair first ) map hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair second ) map share table-at out gladiator-depth-at * to rise
	[ out out height gladiator-height-at rise + lead lead trailing - share * - ] ;

\ the point on a wing's underside the same way
: gladiator-underside ( out share leading height -- point )
	| out share leading height |
	out leading gladiator-edges-at to trailing to lead
	[ out out height gladiator-height-at lead lead trailing - share * - ] ;

\ the ribs' distances out, from a wing's root to the tip's end, nearer together round the tip
: gladiator-rib-stations ( root -- stations )
	| root |
	[ root ] [ 0.13 0.22 0.26 0.75 1.0 1.25 1.5 2.05 2.6 3.2 3.8 4.25 4.46 4.63 4.76 4.86 4.91 4.94 ] ( station | station root > ) filter concat ;

\ the ailerons on all four wings from 1.9 m out to 4.5 m, and the split flaps inboard of them from 0.6 m on the upper wing and from the root cut-out's end on the lower, both hinged at 75% of the chord (the ailerons' ends from the plan view, the flaps and the hinges estimates)
0.6 constant gladiator-flap-inner
1.9 constant gladiator-aileron-inner
4.5 constant gladiator-aileron-outer
0.75 constant gladiator-hinge-share

\ one wing on both sides: a rib at every station from its root, the Clark YH upper surface over the flat underside, the skin filled between the ribs above and below, the tip closed by its last rib, the root closed with a face where it stands clear of the fuselage; the ailerons' hinges and ends on the upper surface and the flaps' on the lower; a Type B roundel 3.2 m out on the upper surface where asked
: sketch-gladiator-wing ( sketch leading height root roundels -- )
	| sketch leading height root roundels |
	hurricane-rib-profile ( pair | pair first ) map to shares
	shares size to n-shares
	root gladiator-rib-stations to stations
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		stations ( out | sketch shares ( share | side out * share leading height gladiator-skin ) map sketch-points ) map to uppers
		stations ( out | sketch shares ( share | side out * share leading height gladiator-underside ) map sketch-points ) map to lowers
		uppers ( rib | sketch rib join-path ) each
		sketch uppers ( rib | rib first ) map join-path
		sketch uppers ( rib | rib last ) map join-path
		0 stations size 1- 1 do r
			stations r @i stations r 1+ @i + 2 / side * to middle-out
			middle-out 0.3 leading height gladiator-skin middle-out 0.3 leading height gladiator-underside v+ 0.5 v* to inside
			0 n-shares 1- 1 do j
				sketch [ uppers r @i j @i uppers r @i j 1+ @i uppers r 1+ @i j 1+ @i uppers r 1+ @i j @i ] inside sketch-face
				sketch [ lowers r @i j @i lowers r @i j 1+ @i lowers r 1+ @i j 1+ @i lowers r 1+ @i j @i ] inside sketch-face
			loop
		loop
		root 0 > if sketch uppers first lowers first reverse concat [ side 0.8 * height 0.05 + leading 0.8 - ] sketch-face then
		root 0 > if gladiator-cut-out-span else gladiator-flap-inner then to flap-inner
		[ [ gladiator-aileron-inner gladiator-aileron-outer 1 ] [ flap-inner gladiator-aileron-inner -1 ] ] ( span |
			span spread to face to outer to inner
			[ inner outer ] ( out | face 0 > if side out * gladiator-hinge-share leading height gladiator-skin [ 0 0.005 0 ] v+ else side out * gladiator-hinge-share leading height gladiator-underside [ 0 -0.005 0 ] v+ then ) map to hinge
			sketch hinge sketch-path
			[ inner outer ] ( out |
				face 0 > if side out * 1 leading height gladiator-skin side out * gladiator-hinge-share leading height gladiator-skin else side out * 1 leading height gladiator-underside side out * gladiator-hinge-share leading height gladiator-underside then
				2 array ( point | point [ 0 face 0.005 * 0 ] v+ ) map to ends
				sketch ends sketch-path
			) each
		) each
		roundels if
			sketch side 3.2 * [ hurricane-roundel-radius hurricane-roundel-centre-radius ] [ roundel-blue-colour roundel-red-colour ]
			leading height ' gladiator-skin 2curry leading ' gladiator-edges-at curry sketch-wing-roundel
		then
	) each ;

\ the two wings: the upper one piece across the fuselage, the lower from its root 0.42 m out, inside the fuselage's side, so the root rib stays hidden where the fuselage's lower half rounds in
