\ the interplane struts, a parallel pair each side 2.05 m out as the plan view places them, streamlined bars 5 cm across and 12 cm fore and aft, leaning forward 30° with the stagger: from the lower wing at 13% and 67% of its chord up to the upper wing at 5% and 58% of its, where the side view draws them; the cabane, a strut each side from the fuselage's round deck 0.35 m out, its foot sunk 4 cm inside the skin, up and out to the upper wing 0.55 m out, each a filled bar 5 cm thick and 12 cm fore and aft without lines of its own, since a bar's end rectangle would draw through the skin, the front one from 1.18 m forward to 1.32 m and the rear from 0.33 m to 0.49 m, between where the two side views draw them; the flying wires from the lower wing's roots up to the upper wing at the struts and the landing wires from the cabane's heads down to the lower wing there, as lines (the wires' places estimates)
