\ the windscreen, a low wedge as the side and front views draw it: two side panels and a flat centre panel 0.16 m wide between them, sloping at 42° from the hoop's crown down to the deck 0.16 m forward of the origin, its two edges the parallel bars the front view shows; each panel's rear edge the hood's front hoop's own arc, from the roof's corner 0.28 m aft to the sill line 0.17 m aft, its lower edge along the sill line and up the deck to the apex, its top edge from the centre panel's foot up to the roof's corner, rounded there into the roof, and a light brace from the hoop's arc a third of the way up to that edge 0.89 m up; the panels glazed, the lower edges along the skin left undrawn; the sliding hood behind it in two panes, its front hoop a band 6 cm wide, 0.28 to 0.34 m aft at the roof and bowed 11 cm forward at the sills, a thin frame between the panes 0.50 m aft, and behind the rear pane a band 8 cm wide, 0.76 to 0.84 m aft; 0.60 m wide at the sills and 0.16 m across the crown, its roof flat at 1.05 m; behind the panes the fixed rear window to the rear frame 1.30 m aft, narrower by 4 cm each side so the hood slides back over it, its top stepping down to 1.03 m and curving to 0.96 m, the start of the headrest fairing's curve; the sills 0.58 m up on the round decking's shoulders, 4 cm below its crown, so the hood's sides cut into it; the frames' stations and the sill line from the side views, the widths from the plan view
0.58 constant gladiator-sill-height
0.11 constant gladiator-hoop-bow
\ the hood's hoops, each an arch of fourteen points from sill to sill, seven a side at even shares of its rise, 0.60 m wide at the sills, its sides leaning in steeply, 0.42 m across at 55% of its rise and 0.28 m at 85%, to a crown 0.16 m across, as the front view draws it: [ along top narrowing bow ], the bow how far forward of the station the sills stand; a bowed hoop is a smooth arc convex aft, leaving the roof's corner 0.27 of the bow aft per unit of fall and curving forward below, so that it passes 0.03 of the bow aft of the station at mid-height
